===Verb===
{{en-verb}}
[[File:Hilda Dokubo crying 1.jpg|thumb|A woman crying (1)]]

# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[shed a tear|shed tears]]; to [[weep]]. Especially in [[anger]] or [[sadness]]
#: {{ux|en|That sad movie always makes me '''cry'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|This heart-breaking moment gets me '''crying.'''}}
#: {{ux|en|That made me '''cried''' when I been traumatized about suicidal thoughts.}}
#: {{ux|en|If somebody '''cries''' in a bathtub they saw a ghost.}}
#* {{quote-video game|en|author=Sonic Team|title=Sonic Battle|publisher=Sega|year=2003|year_published=2003|system=Game Boy Advance|level=Cream’s Story|text= - Emerl: “There’s nothing worse than making a girl '''cry'''!” That’s what Sonic said...}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To utter loudly; to call out; to declare publicly.
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Othello|act=V|scene=ii|passage=All, all, '''cry''' shame against ye, yet I'll speak.}}
#* {{RQ:Bunyan Pilgrim's Progress|page=3|passage=[T]he Man put his fingers in his Ears, and ran on '''crying''', Life, Life, Eternal Life: [...]}}
# {{lb|en|ambitransitive}} To [[shout]], [[scream]], [[yell]].
#* {{RQ:King James Version|Matthew|27|46|passage=And about the ninth hour, Jesus '''cried''' with a loud voice.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive|figuratively}} To [[forcefully]] [[attract]] [[attention]] or [[proclaim]] one’s [[presence]].
#* {{RQ:Roethke Collected|Open House|3|My secrets '''cry''' aloud.<br>I have no need for tongue.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To utter inarticulate sounds, as animals do.
#* {{RQ:King James Version|Psalms|147|9||the young ravens which '''cry'''}}
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Tempest|act=V|scene=i|passage=In a cowslip's bell I lie / There I couch when owls do '''cry'''.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To cause to do something, or bring to some state, by crying or weeping.
#: {{ux|en|Tonight I’ll '''cry''' myself to sleep.}}
# To make [[oral]] and [[public]] [[proclamation]] of; to [[notify]] or [[advertise]] by [[outcry]], especially things lost or [[found]], goods to be [[sold]], [[auction]]ed, etc.
#: {{ux|en|to '''cry''' goods}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1652|author={{w|W|Richard Crashaw}}|title=The Beginning of Heliodorus
|passage=Love is lost, and thus she '''cries''' him.}}
#* {{RQ:Pynchon Crying of Lot 49|year=1976|chapter=6|page=137|passage=“We're in luck. Loren Passerine, the finest auctioneer in the West, will be '''crying''' today.” “Will be what?” “We say an auctioneer ‘cries’ a sale,” Cohen said.}}
#* {{quote-song|en|year=1976|author={{w|Stan Rogers}}|title={{w|Barrett's Privateers}}|album=''{{w|Fogarty's Cove}}''|text=Oh, Elcid Barrett '''cried''' the town / (How I wish I was in Sherbrooke now!) / For twenty brave men, all fishermen, who / Would make for him the ''Antelope's'' crew.}}
## Hence, to publish the [[banns]] of, as for marriage.
##* {{quote-text|en|year=1845|author=w:Sylvester Judd|title=Margaret: A Tale of the Real and the Ideal, Blight and Bloom; Including Sketches of a Place Not Before Described, Called Mons Christi
|passage=I should not be surprised if they were '''cried''' in church next Sabbath.}}

